    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d433">

                <pb facs="0426" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/2069: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-06T17:00:00+03:25">December 6, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 6—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1091. Declaration as to Iran was enthusiastically received by group of Cabinet
                    members, deputies, Army leaders, and press representatives to whom Prime
                    Minister announced it yesterday. My 1090, December 5.<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d433-f1"/> Deputy Teheri made fulsome speech in praise of Allied
                    chiefs, thanking them for this demonstration of friendship and respect for Iran.
                    Today’s Tehran papers unanimously echo this enthusiasm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
